%%{init: {'sequence': {'wrap': true}}}%%
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    box Curator ring
    actor CurOp as Curator operator<br/>(upgrade authority)
    participant CurRing as Curator ring program
    end
    box Chain state
    participant CurPC as Curator PolicyConfig
    participant SubPC as Subscriber PolicyConfig
    end
    box Subscriber ring
    participant SubRing as Subscriber ring program
    actor SubOp as Subscriber operator<br/>(upgrade authority)
    end

    rect rgba(128, 128, 128, 0.07)
    Note over CurOp, CurPC: the curator provisions first, the cli refuses a curator not serving Block before the pin and the program refuses it with CuratorSourceMissing
    CurOp->>CurRing: create_config, init_spp_ring_config
    CurOp->>+CurRing: create_policy, the rows from ring.toml, Block reads its own namespace PDA
    CurRing->>-CurPC: stores the rows and the map, policy_hash binds all eight slots, generation 1
    end

    rect rgba(128, 128, 128, 0.07)
    SubOp->>+SubRing: create_policy, the rows from ring.toml, sources = [(Block, curator policy config)]
    SubRing->>CurPC: reads the curator's resolved namespace owner
    Note right of SubRing: copies the RESOLVED address, delegation does not chain, the entries tree must equal the curator's
    SubRing->>-SubPC: stores the rows and the map, policy_hash binds both, generation 1
    end

    Note over CurOp, SubOp: create_policy and set_policy_rules sign with the upgrade authority, set_policy_source with the config authority, each write repins the hash at the next generation
